# Recorded declaration evidence schema

Import AlejandroJsonFields from "./alejandro_json_fields.lg".
Import AlejandroEvidencePolicy from "./alejandro_evidence_policy.lg".

## To validateAlejandroDeclaration (row: Json) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Let texts be ["lean", "lean_kind", "lean_type", "status", "test", "logos", "why"].
    Inspect alejandroTextFields(row, texts, ["lean_levels", "lean_axioms"], ["refusal"]):
        When Err (problem):
            Return a new Err with error problem.
        When Ok (values):
            Let name be item 1 of values.
            If name is equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error "empty original declaration name".
            Let kind be item 2 of values.
            If alejandroRecordedChoice(kind, ["def", "theorem", "opaque", "inductive", "ctor", "axiom", "rec"]) is equal to false:
                Return a new Err with error "unknown original declaration kind".
            If alejandroRecordedChoice(item 4 of values, ["bridged", "open", "refused"]) is equal to false:
                Return a new Err with error "unknown recorded ledger status".
            If jsonHas(row, "refusal"):
                Inspect jsonRequireObject(jsonGet(row, "refusal")):
                    When Err (failure):
                        Return a new Err with error "recorded refusal must be an object".
            Return a new Ok with value name.
    Return a new Err with error "invalid declaration observation".
